{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1103393-what-level-celerity-are-the-vampires-in-the-originals-using","id":1103393,"title":"What level celerity are the vampires in the Originals using?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-13T22:48:11-07:00","id":1103393,"title":"What level celerity are the vampires in the Originals using?","content":"From the show &quot;The Originals&quot;. If you guys watch it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T06:38:43-07:00","id":1103463,"title":"","content":"Celerity 1.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing about Celerity. From an outside perspective, it almost looks like teleportation. One second you're there, the next second you're across the room. At each level, you can move farther, but it doesn't change the outside perspective. Vampire disciplines, as a whole, are designed to be monstrous from the word go. You're going to be doing classic monster-movie style abilities from the very start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T10:08:17-07:00","id":1103539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1103393-what-level-celerity-are-the-vampires-in-the-originals-using?p=1103463#post1103463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celerity 1.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing about Celerity. From an outside perspective, it almost looks like teleportation. One second you're there, the next second you're across the room. At each level, you can move farther, but it doesn't change the outside perspective. Vampire disciplines, as a whole, are designed to be monstrous from the word go. You're going to be doing classic monster-movie style abilities from the very start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow only celerity 1?<br /> <br /> In the game &quot;Vampire the Masquerade: Bloodlines&quot;, you can use Celerity 1 in public without any repercussions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T10:18:50-07:00","id":1103542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1103393-what-level-celerity-are-the-vampires-in-the-originals-using?p=1103539#post1103539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow only celerity 1?<br /> <br /> In the game &amp;quot;Vampire the Masquerade: Bloodlines&amp;quot;, you can use Celerity 1 in public without any repercussions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bloodlines has slightly different mechanics from Masquerade in account of it being a video game version. And Masquerade has slightly different mechanics than Requiem on account of it being a different game entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T18:50:48-07:00","id":1103682,"title":"","content":"So a vampire with celerity 1 can snap multiple people's neck before they can even react?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T19:04:38-07:00","id":1103684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1103393-what-level-celerity-are-the-vampires-in-the-originals-using?p=1103682#post1103682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a vampire with celerity 1 can snap multiple people's neck before they can even react?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as such within the rules of CofD combat, which only allows one action per turn. But, if they're just random mooks that pose no real threat to the vampire, you could resolve the scene with Down and Dirty Combat, and at that point you could certainly narrate it as the vampire snapping all of their necks before they can react.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-14-2017, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T06:55:45-07:00","id":1103789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1103393-what-level-celerity-are-the-vampires-in-the-originals-using?p=1103682#post1103682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a vampire with celerity 1 can snap multiple people's neck before they can even react?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of? <br /> <br /> Any amount of Celerity lets you pre-emptively use your action before another person. So, Celerity 1, spend a point of vitae to go before anyone else, then make a grapple check. On a success, you get to do a damage move. Which, with enough strength / vigor, can be interpreted to snap a neck. <br /> <br /> So, its a bit more complicated than just Celerity 1 to snap a neck (since actual snapping probably needs frenzy bonus, blood buffing, Vigor, etc), but the actual &quot;I'm there, got you by the neck&quot; part? Absolutely possible with just Celerity 1<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}